Z||000000||Rodney||05-12-2000||09:17 AM||||My source for the low temp fan switches is gone. They can only get a newer style which would require you to cut the factory end off the wiring harness and crimp on a new end. I don't think too many people would want to do that. I have been working with a few companies trying to get some produced with the correct connector. I had one who said they could do it but reciently said they could not get the correct connector. So I am trying with some other sources. I feel I will be able to get them done but it will take some time. Maybe mid summer? Untill then I am out of stock on the 185-200 fan switches.<P>Rodney Dickman ||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||05-12-2000||10:50 AM||||Is the old style connector a weather packed one? GM, and pretty much everyone else, has eliminated most of the older non weather pack stuff. You have the same problem with the ECM coolant sensor. If you replace the ECM coolant sensor you have to upgrade the harness to the new conector. (Borg Warner includes the connector and small instructions with the new ECM sensor. Some other's don't.)<P>IF you can't get the old fan connector, then what I would do is put the new connector in parallel with the old one, not cut it off. This way you could put the stock one back if need be. To protect the old connector from corrosion pack it with some dielectric grease and tie it back against the harness so it can't get into anything.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-12-2000).]||||reg||1
